class.description:
A [KinematicBody] (through [CellPlayerBody], so it also waits for streamed ground and can shove a [CellItemBody]) that moves itself every physics frame: the horizontal velocity eases toward [member move_input], gravity pulls it down while it is off the floor, and [member view_input] turns [member yaw_node] and [member pitch_node]. It never reads the keyboard or the mouse. Game code sets [member move_input], feeds mouse motion to [member view_input] or [method add_view_input], calls [method jump], and changes [member max_speed] for walk / run / sprint. The step runs after the script's own [code]_physics_process[/code], so what a script sets in a tick is what the body moves with in that tick. To run the step at another point, turn [member movement_enabled] and [member view_enabled] off and call [method process_movement] and [method process_view] yourself. [codeblock] extends CellCharacterBody
func _unhandled_input(event): if event is InputEventMouseMotion: add_view_input(-event.relative) if event.is_action_pressed("jump"): jump()
func _physics_process(_delta): move_input = Input.get_vector("strafe_left", "strafe_right", "move_forward", "move_backward") max_speed = 7.2 if Input.is_action_pressed("sprint") else 4.26 [/codeblock]
